<title>JAPAN: DSL Bank launches 3.0% reverse yen/A$ samurai.</title>
<headline>DSL Bank launches 3.0% reverse yen/A$ samurai.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following reverse yen/Australian dollar dual-currency samurai bond issue was announced by lead-manager Nomura Securities on Wednesday:</p>
<p> BORROWER	  DSL Bank Deutsche Siedlungs-und</p>
<p>			Landesrentenbank</p>
<p> AMT		 15 bln yen</p>
<p> COUPON	    3.0 pct</p>
<p> ISS PRICE	 par</p>
<p> MATURITY	  15 May 2007</p>
<p> PAY DATE	  15 May 1997</p>
<p> SUB PERIOD	May 14</p>
<p> PAY FREQ	  Annual</p>
<p> LAST RATING     Moody's Aaa, IBCA AAA</p>
<p> LEAD MANAGER    Nomura Securities</p>
<p> LEAD TRUSTEE    Fuji Bank</p>
<p>NOTE: The exchange rate was fixed at A$5,042.86 per 500,000 yen. -- Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-8785</p>
</text>
